c/Vvw3ms","and he bowed down"],["יִשְׂרָאֵל","yisra'el","H3478","HNpm","Israel"],["עַל","'al-","H5921","HR","on"],["רֹאשׁ","rosh","H7218","HNcmsc","[the] head of"],["הַמִּטָּה","hamitah","H4296","HTd/Ncfsa","the bed"]],"x":[[11001047,11001047,5],[1024003,1024003,4],[58011021,58011021,4]],"xn":3}},"people":[{"id":"joseph_1710","name":"Joseph","also":"Zaphnath-paaneah","summary":"The elder of the two sons of Jacob by Rachel (Gen. 30:23, 24), who, on the occasion of his birth, said, “God hath taken away [Heb. ‘asaph] my reproach.”","verses":199,"father":"Israel","mother":"Rachel","v":[1,5,7,11,12,14,15,16,17,20,23,26,29]},{"id":"canaan_914","name":"Canaan","also":"Canaanites, Canaanite","summary":"The fourth son of Ham (Gen. 10:6). His descendants were under a curse in consequence of the transgression of his father (9:22-27). His eldest son, Zidon, was the father of the Sidonians and Phoenicians.","verses":84,"father":"Ham","mother":"","v":[1,4,13,14,15]},{"id":"pharaoh_2329","name":"Pharaoh","also":"","summary":"The Pharaoh of Joseph’s days (Gen. 41) was probably Apopi, or Apopis, the last of the Hyksos kings. To the old native Egyptians, who were an African race, shepherds were “an abomination;” but to the Hyksos kings these Asiatic shepherds who now appeared with Jacob at their head were congenial, and being akin to their own race, had a warm welcome (Gen. 47:5, 6).","verses":63,"father":"","mother":"","v":[1,2,3,4,5,7,8,9,10,11,19,20,22,23,24,26]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[7,8,9,10,27,28,29,31]},{"id":"pharaoh_2331","name":"Pharaoh","also":"","summary":"The Pharaoh of the Exodus was probably Menephtah I., the fourteenth and eldest surviving son of Rameses II. He resided at Zoan, where he had the various interviews with Moses and Aaron recorded in the book of Exodus.","verses":138,"father":"","mother":"","v":[14,20,25,26]}],"places":[{"id":"canaan_272","name":"Canaan","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":31.69353,"lon":34.84388,"summary":"The country which derived its name from the preceding. The name as first used by the Phoenicians denoted only the maritime plain on which Sidon was built.","verses":76,"v":[1,4,13,14,15]},{"id":"goshen_490","name":"Goshen","kind":"Region","lat":30.7285,"lon":31.80469,"summary":"A district in Egypt where Jacob and his family settled, and in which they remained till the Exodus (Gen. 45:10; 46:28, 29, 31, etc.). It is called “the land of Goshen” (47:27), and also simply “Goshen” (46:28), and “the land of Rameses” (47:11; Ex. 12:37), for the towns Pithom and Rameses lay within its borders; also Zoan or Tanis (Ps. 78:12).","verses":11,"v":[1,4,6,27]},{"id":"egypt_362","name":"Egypt","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":26.4902,"lon":29.8808,"summary":"The land of the Nile and the pyramids, the oldest kingdom of which we have any record, holds a place of great significance in Scripture.","verses":564,"v":[6,11,13,14,15,20,21,26,27,28,29,30]},{"id":"rameses_980","name":"Rameses","kind":"City","lat":30.79937,"lon":31.83422,"summary":"“the land of” (Gen. 47:11), was probably “the land of Goshen” 45:10.","verses":4,"v":[11]}],"events":[{"id":"death_of_jacob_116","title":"Death of Jacob","year":-1689,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 47:28–49:31. People: Israel. Place: Egypt.","v":[28]}],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[3130,3130,935,5046,5046,6547,1,1,251,251,251,6629,6629,6629,1241,1241,3605,3605,834,834,935,935,776,776,776,3667,3667,2005,2005,2005,1657,1657],[3947,3947,3947,2568,582,251,251,3322,3322,3322,6440,6547],[4100,4639,4639,4639,6547,559,251,251,5650,5650,7462,7462,559,559,1571,587,1571,1,1],[559,559,559,413,6547,935,935,935,776,776,776,776,776